.TH VV 1 "October 2026" "vv 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vv \- polite command line wrapper with completion alerts and timing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vv
is a wrapper around command line tasks to make them run politely in the background (using \fBnice\fR and \fBionice\fR), measure resource utilization (via \fB/usr/bin/time -v\fR), synchronize filesystem caches, and notify the user via audio cues and desktop notifications upon completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH USAGE
Simply prepend \fBvv\fR to your command:
.PP
.nf
.RS
vv apt-get upgrade -y
vv make -j4
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B VV_NICENESS
CPU scheduling priority applied via \fBnice -n\fR (default: 19).
.TP
.B VV_IO_NICENESS
I/O scheduling class applied via \fBionice -c\fR (default: 3).
.TP
.B VV_SYNC
Perform filesystem \fBsync\fR after command execution. Set to \fB0\fR to skip (default: 1).
.TP
.B VV_NOTIFY
Send desktop notification on completion via \fBnotify-send\fR or \fBosascript\fR. Set to \fB0\fR to disable (default: 1).
.TP
.B VV_BELL
Emit terminal bell if no audio player or sound file is available. Set to \fB0\fR to disable (default: 1).
.TP
.B VV_PLAYER
Explicit audio player executable (e.g. \fIaplay -q\fR, \fIpaplay\fR, \fIpw-play\fR, \fImpv\fR).
.TP
.B VV_PLAYFILE
Override sound file to play upon completion.
.TP
.B VV_SUCCESS_SOUND
Sound file to play when the command exits with status 0.
.TP
.B VV_FAILURE_SOUND
Sound file to play when the command exits with non-zero status.
.TP
.B VV_PRE
Prefix command to wrap target execution, overriding automatic nice/ionice/time construction.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vv/config
Primary XDG configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.vv/config
Fallback configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.vvrc
Legacy fallback configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fBvv\fR propagates the exit status of the executed command. If invoked with invalid arguments or without a command, it exits with status 1.
